        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can you apply polyaspartic over old epoxy?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Yes, with conditions. If the existing epoxy coating is fully adhered, clean, and not peeling, you can apply a polyaspartic topcoat over it — but you must first scuff-sand the entire surface with 80-grit sandpaper or a floor buffer with sanding screens to create mechanical adhesion. Polyaspartic applied directly over smooth, glossy cured epoxy without sanding will delaminate. If the existing epoxy is peeling or was applied over a contaminated surface, remove it completely before applying any new coating. The integrity of the bond between polyaspartic and the substrate is only as strong as the weakest layer in the coating stack.",
