          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "The standard recommendation is to apply the second coat or topcoat within the recoat window specified by the manufacturer — typically 12–24 hours after the base coat for epoxy products. Applying within this window while the base coat is in its \"green\" (partially cured) state allows chemical bonding between coats, which produces much stronger inter-coat adhesion than waiting for the base coat to fully cure. If you miss the recoat window and the base coat has fully cured, you must scuff-sand the surface before applying the next coat to create mechanical adhesion. Always check the specific recoat window in the product instructions, as it varies by product chemistry and temperature.",
          },
        },
